-- title:
--   Ordinary line at p‖M in a p-new quotient of TₚJ₁(M)
-- statement:
--   Fix a nonzero natural number $M$ and a prime $p$ with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, a finite set $S \subseteq \mathbb{N}$, and a field $K$ carrying a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra structure. For a level $N$, write $J_1(N)$ for $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the function field of $X_1(N)$, with its coefficientwise Galois action and the action of [`ModularCurve.HeckeAlgOne`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L16) $= \mathbb{Z}[X_\ell \ (\ell \text{ prime}),\, Y_d \ (d \in \mathbb{N})]$ supplied by [`ModularCurve.heckeModuleOneBar`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L129) (taken at levels $M$ and $M/p$), and $T_p J_1(N)$ for the $p$-adic Tate module, i.e. the group of sequences $(x_n)$ in $J_1(N)$ with $p^n x_n = 0$ and $p x_{n+1} = x_n$, with the induced actions of Galois and of the Hecke polynomial ring. Let $A_1 =$ `rationalHeckeAlgebraOne` be the $\mathbb{Q}_p$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{Q}_p}(\mathbb{Q}_p \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p} T_p J_1(M))$ generated by the image of the Hecke polynomial ring. The assertion is: for every ring homomorphism $\Lambda \colon A_1 \to K$ that carries $\mathbb{Z}_p \subseteq \mathbb{Q}_p$ to $K$ via the given algebra map, such that $\Lambda(\langle \ell \rangle) = 1$ for every prime $\ell \nmid M$ with $\ell \notin S$ and $\ell \equiv 1 \pmod{M/p}$ (here $\langle \ell \rangle$ denotes the image of $Y_\ell$), and for every $a \in K$ with $\Lambda(\langle \ell \rangle)\, a = \Lambda(T_p)$ for every prime $\ell \nmid M$ with $\ell \notin S$ and $\ell \equiv p \pmod{M/p}$ ($T_p$ being the image of $X_p$), the following holds. Let $W$ be a $K$-vector space with $\dim_K W = 2$, let $r$ be any function from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}) = \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \simeq_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{alg}} \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ to $\mathrm{End}_K(W)$ (no multiplicativity is assumed), and let $\pi \colon K \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p} T_p J_1(M) \to W$ be a surjective $K$-linear map intertwining the base-changed Galois action with $r$ and sending the base-changed action of each Hecke polynomial $t$ to multiplication by $\Lambda$ of the corresponding element of $A_1$. Assume further the $p$-newness condition: every $K$-linear map $f \colon K \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p} T_p J_1(M/p) \to W$ satisfying $f(X_\ell z) = \Lambda(T_\ell) f(z)$ and $f(Y_\ell z) = \Lambda(\langle \ell \rangle) f(z)$ for all primes $\ell \nmid M$ with $\ell \notin S$ is zero. Finally let $P$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $p$, in the sense that $p$ is a nonunit of $P$. Then there is a $K$-submodule $L \subseteq W$ with $\dim_K L \le 1$ such that $L$ is stable under $r \sigma$ for every $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, such that $r \tau (w) - w \in L$ for every $\tau$ in the image in $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ of the inertia subgroup of $P$ and every $w \in W$, and such that $r \sigma (w) - a w \in L$ for every $w \in W$ and every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $P$ and inducing $x \mapsto x^p$ on the residue field of $P$.
--
--   This is the statement that the $p$-adic representation cut out by a $p$-new Hecke character $\Lambda$ of level $M$ with $p \| M$ is ordinary at $p$ in the strong, multiplicative form: inertia at $p$ acts trivially modulo a line stable under the decomposition group, on which Frobenius acts through the scalar $a = \Lambda(U_p \langle p \rangle^{-1})$ read off from the second hypothesis. It feeds the construction of the ordinary line for the $\lambda$-adic representation of a primitive form, in [`CuspForm.IsPrimitiveForm.exists_galoisRepAdic_ordinaryLine_frobenius_sub_qCoeff_smul_mem_of_dvd_of_not_sq_dvd_of_not_dvd_conductor`](thm.html#CuspForm.IsPrimitiveForm.exists_galoisRepAdic_ordinaryLine_frobenius_sub_qCoeff_smul_mem_of_dvd_of_not_sq_dvd_of_not_dvd_conductor).
